Capsule
=======

Capsule is free software, released under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 (see LICENSE).

It builds on the work of others:

PokeDaisy  -  https://pokedaisy.com  -  https://github.com/lidor30/pokedaisy
  The game runs on PokeDaisy's libretro core (pokedaisy_gbc_libretro): mGBA
  with PokeDaisy's companion, HUD, quick menu, EXPAND and field shortcuts built
  in. Copyright (c) PokeDaisy's authors. GNU GPL v3. It is not copied into this
  repository: scripts/build_core.sh downloads a pinned revision of our fork,
  https://github.com/louislovni/pokedaisy (branch capsule: upstream PokeDaisy
  plus Capsule's changes, listed in its CAPSULE.md, under the same GPL v3).
  Its own NOTICE lists what it bundles.
  Core/pkcore/pk_profiles_gen.c (per-game memory addresses) is generated from
  PokeDaisy's gamedata by tools/gen_profiles.py.
  Capsule is not made or endorsed by PokeDaisy's authors.

DSperate  -  https://github.com/lidor30/pokedaisy (third_party/dsperate-lr)
  The Nintendo DS emulator inside PokeDaisy's DS core (pokedaisy_ds_libretro),
  built without its JIT. GNU GPL v3. Fetched by PokeDaisy's build; the fork
  changes its 3D engine for EXPAND (third_party/patches/dsperate-capsule.patch).

mGBA  -  https://mgba.io  -  https://github.com/mgba-emu/mgba
  The emulator inside PokeDaisy's core. Copyright (c) Jeffrey Pfau and
  contributors. Mozilla Public License 2.0. Fetched by PokeDaisy's build.

pret disassemblies  -  https://github.com/pret/pokered, https://github.com/pret/pokecrystal
  Core/pkcore/pk_gbdata_gen.c (base stats, species order, items, places of the
  Game Boy games) is generated from them by tools/gen_gbdata.py, and Core/pkcore/pk_gb.c
  follows their save layout and formulas.

PokeAPI  -  https://github.com/PokeAPI/pokeapi
  French names of species, moves, items and places in Core/pkcore/pk_gbdata_gen.c.
  Copyright (c) 2013-2023 Paul Hallett and PokeAPI contributors. BSD 3-Clause
  licence: redistribution in source and binary forms is permitted provided the
  copyright notice, this list of conditions and the disclaimer are retained;
  the software is provided "as is", without any warranty; the PokeAPI name may
  not be used to endorse derived products.

pret decompilation projects  -  https://github.com/pret
  The documentation of the Generation 3 data structures and save format that
  Core/pkcore implements.

Capsule contains no game, no BIOS and no game asset. Pokemon and Game Boy
Advance are trademarks of their respective owners; this project is not
affiliated with or endorsed by them.

PKHeX  -  https://github.com/kwsch/PKHeX
  GPL v3. Reference for the DS save layouts (generations 4 and 5); French
  names of species, moves, abilities, items, types and locations, and the
  generation 4 character table (tools/gen_ndsdata.py); four sample Pokemon
  files used by Core/tests/test_pknds.c.

xdelta3  -  https://github.com/jmacd/xdelta
  Core/third_party/xdelta3: its decoder applies .xdelta ROM patches (the hack
  patcher). Copyright Joshua MacDonald. Apache License 2.0. Unchanged; built
  decode-only by Core/third_party/xd3_capsule.c.

XZ Embedded  -  https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz-embedded
  Core/third_party/xz-embedded: the LZMA2 decoder behind xdelta3's LZMA
  compression, through Core/third_party/xz-shim. Copyright the XZ Embedded
  authors. Zero-clause BSD: use, copy, modify and distribute freely.

Monocypher 4.0.2  -  https://monocypher.org  -  https://github.com/LoupVaillant/Monocypher
  Core/third_party/monocypher: its X25519, for the co-op link's Noise
  handshake (Core/coop). Copyright (c) 2017-2023 Loup Vaillant, Michael Savage,
  Fabio Scotoni. Dual-licensed BSD 2-Clause or CC0 1.0 (LICENCE.md beside it).
  Unchanged.

mdns  -  https://github.com/mjansson/mdns (commit a569c47)
  Core/third_party/mdns/mdns.h: the Windows build's LAN discovery for the
  co-op link (windows/coop_pc.c). By Mattias Jansson. Public domain
  (Unlicense, LICENSE beside it). Unchanged.

The co-op link (Core/coop) speaks PokeDaisy's co-op protocol (its Android
app's CoopNoise, CoopChannel, CoopWire, CoopTicket, CoopPairing and
CoopLinkImpl), so Capsule and PokeDaisy devices pair and play together.
